{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.belowCap_index_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.belowCap_index_pos","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L280-L286","doc":"The cap is sharp: at a cell of row `i ≤ N` in column 1 the factor is\n`[N + 1 − i]_q`, whose index is strictly positive, so nothing above the cap is\nkilled by this mechanism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.rowCapFactor_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.rowCapFactor_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L271-L278","doc":"**The row cap is automatic, not imposed.**  At that cell the numerator factor\nis `[N + content]_q = [N − N]_q = [0]_q = 0`, so the whole hook-content weight\nvanishes.  This is `RowCapObstruction.weyl_dim_alt_eq_zero_iff` arriving as\narithmetic rather than as a dimension count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.cap_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.cap_content","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L266-L269","doc":"**The cap cell.**  A partition with more than `N` rows has a cell at\n`(N+1, 1)`, and its content is `−N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.qIntBalanced_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.qIntBalanced_zero","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L263-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.qIntBalanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.qIntBalanced","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L257-L261","doc":"The balanced quantum integer `[m]_q = (q^m − q^{−m})/(q − q⁻¹)`, at integer\n`m`.  This is the factor the hook-content numerator contributes per cell, with\n`m = N + content`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.content","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L253-L255","doc":"The content of the cell in row `i`, column `j` of a Young diagram\n(1-indexed), as an integer: `j − i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.conventionD_forces_rank_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.conventionD_forces_rank_two","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L243-L247","doc":"**No rank other than 2 gives convention D.**  The corollary that matters for\nthe corpus: `z = q³/(q²+1)` pins `N = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_injective","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L235-L241","doc":"**The rank is recoverable from the Markov parameter.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_strictAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_strictAnti","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L217-L233","doc":"**The family is strictly decreasing in the rank.**  Together with\n`markovParam_injective` this is what makes convention D a *rank commitment*:\n`z` determines `N`, so the mass channel's trace cannot be silently retuned to a\ndifferent rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_gt_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_gt_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L202-L207","doc":"Every member of the family lies strictly above the Hecke coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_sub_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_sub_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L191-L200","doc":"**The excess over the Hecke coefficient is exactly the row cap.**\n`z_N − (q − q⁻¹) = (q − q⁻¹)/(q^{2N} − 1)`, strictly positive and strictly\ndecreasing — so an uncapped (`N → ∞`) trace would sit at `q − q⁻¹` and every\nfinite rank sits strictly above it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_three","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L179-L189","doc":"**`z_3 = q⁵/(q⁴+q²+1)`** — the value a flavour `SU(3)` trace on the same\n`H_n(q)` would have to carry.  `≈ 0.4493048091` at the substrate `q₀`.  A\nspecification, not a construction: nothing here builds such a trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_two","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L166-L177","doc":"**`z_2 = q³/(q²+1)` — this is convention D**, the corpus's canonical Markov\nparameter (owner ruling 2026-08-15 R1).  So the production trace is the rank-2\nmember of the family, and `def:quantum-observable-universe`'s condition 5\n`Λ²V ≅ 𝟙` is the same commitment read categorically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam_one","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L157-L164","doc":"**`z_1 = q`** — the `gl(1)` corner, where only the fully symmetric block\nsurvives.  (`N = 1` keeps exactly the partitions with one row.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.heckeCoeff_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.heckeCoeff_pos","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L144-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.denom_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.denom_pos","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L141-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.one_lt_pow_two_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.one_lt_pow_two_mul","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L137-L139","doc":"`1 < q^{2N}` for `N ≥ 1` — what makes the denominator non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L135-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.q_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.q_pos","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.heckeCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.heckeCoeff","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L123-L125","doc":"The Hecke coefficient `q − q⁻¹` — the `N → ∞` value of the family, and the\ncoefficient in `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OcneanuRankFamily.markovParam","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OcneanuRankFamily.lean#L114-L121","doc":"The Markov parameter of the rank-`N` Ocneanu / Wenzl trace, as a closed form\nin the substrate modulus.\n\n`z_N = (q − q⁻¹) · q^{2N} / (q^{2N} − 1)`.  See the module docstring for its\nprovenance: it is the value of `tr_M(σ)` on the hook-content weights of\n`computations/y_lambda_su_n.py`, verified symbolically for `N = 1 … 6`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}